  "term": "Stanford Hypnotic Susceptibility Scale",
  "definition": "The Stanford Hypnotic Susceptibility Scale, Form C, is a measure of how responsive a person is to hypnosis. It assesses responses across three broad areas: direct motor suggestions, reduced voluntary motor control, and suggested changes in perception, memory, and thinking.",
